# Copy to .env and fill in. Only .env is read; keys in your shell are ignored.
# Every key is optional, as long as something can hear, think and speak: TARS uses the services there are keys for and
# says at startup what it does without the others (voice-assistant --check shows it too).
# OpenAI: answers what needs the web, the thinking model, and backs up speech to text; hears and speaks without
# Deepgram, and answers everything without Groq or Cerebras. platform.openai.com
OPENAI_API_KEY=
# Deepgram: [stt] provider = "deepgram" or "flux" (OpenAI's otherwise); also the voice, with [tts] provider =
# "deepgram" or without a Cartesia key. console.deepgram.com
DEEPGRAM_API_KEY=
# Cartesia: the voice, [tts] provider = "cartesia" with a Sonic model and cartesia_voice; Deepgram's or OpenAI's
# otherwise. play.cartesia.ai
CARTESIA_API_KEY=
# Groq: [llm] groq_model, the quick brain; console.groq.com
GROQ_API_KEY=
# Cerebras: [llm] cerebras_model, the quick brain when Groq can't answer (or the only one); cloud.cerebras.ai
CEREBRAS_API_KEY=
# Home Assistant: a long-lived access token, for [home] (the lock and the boiler). In Home Assistant: your profile,
# Security, Long-lived access tokens. docs/home.md
HOME_ASSISTANT_TOKEN=
# The IR blaster's local key, for an ac in [home] (python -m tinytuya wizard finds it). docs/home.md
TUYA_LOCAL_KEY=
